<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 78.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg (a, b) = (0.12, 0.88) on a periodic 22-wavelength patch. Du is solved so the linear fastest wavelength is 1.803 µm at r/r_c = 1.06. At that fixed Du, predecessor D. deflecta (r/r_c = 2.65) selects 2.196 µm and successor D. erecta (r/r_c = 1.48) selects 1.940 µm. Continuous-versus-stencil dispersion Pearson r = 0.991, RMSE = 0.0249. The nonlinear FFT wavelength is 1.669 µm and was not retuned. The green-leaf test G > R+18 returns a foreground fraction of 1.0 because the leaf is yellow (R ≈ G). Age 0 Ma, scale 1.8 µm. Overall 78.8/100 (faithfulness 75.6, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e7f1d7c4b94a5129fd92c9739f2ce6b72bc4ab0f; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0.py at e7f1d7c4b94a5129fd92c9739f2ce6b72bc4ab0f, image/png, 718269 B, 1342×902 px, artifact_sha256 024ce5a6b13189dcceb1a0972eb72bfea6149ca8c200536f3fc9708616680792 (sha256 024ce5a6b13189dcceb1a0972eb72bfea6149ca8c200536f3fc9708616680792), spec_fingerprint a12bb3100b597e414ef74972864fc5e5fa6a02a00d315c7492cd5f4151bd913e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a12bb3100b597e414ef74972864fc5e5fa6a02a00d315c7492cd5f4151bd913e; artifact_sha256: 024ce5a6b13189dcceb1a0972eb72bfea6149ca8c200536f3fc9708616680792; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=92b2e690554d6b38..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_elegans_specimen.jpg=ed8dfe6c85be35e1..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e5d4cbec3c5231fc..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=f3905fa5ed82ba4a..., datasets/drosophila_elegans_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=98aa35f7c02c324d...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yeh, Liou & True 2006: male D. elegans carries an apical wing melanin patch used in courtship, divergent from D. gunungcola. | Turing 1952: diffusion can destabilize a stable homogeneous state at a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here.; reconstructed_in_script: Du is solved so argmax sigma(k) equals 2π/1.803 µm at r/r_c = 1.06. Deflecta and erecta wavelengths are the same law at r/r_c = 2.65 and 1.48.; transfer_boundary: Deflecta and erecta are chronoseries neighbors (11/41), not the sister species in the Yeh and Massey papers.; does_not_claim: The macro photograph does not resolve 1.8 µm granules. | No published granule-spacing measurement for D. deflecta or D. erecta is being reproduced.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Set NONLINEAR_K_CORRECTION from the measured k_nonlinear/k_linear and re-solve Du so the FFT wavelength is within 2.5% of 1.803 µm.",
        "remediation needed: R2: Replace the G>R+18 leaf test, which scored foreground fraction 1.0 on this yellow leaf, with a low-B leaf mask, the largest red-eye component circularity, and a scale-bar calibration in mm.",
        "remediation needed: R3: Sweep r/r_c at fixed Du and show that the linear wavelength changes monotonically.",
        "remediation needed: R4: Simulate the equal-diffusion ablation and report pattern-std/ablation-std together with a two-sample KS statistic.",
        "remediation needed: R5: Report the coefficient of variation of the nonlinear wavelength across seeds." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.88e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila elegans Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.8 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Three chronospecies ratios at fixed Du move the linear wavelength from 1.803 µm (elegans) to 1.940 µm (erecta) to 2.196 µm (deflecta), and that ordering is plotted. There is no sweep across the ratio range and no simulated equal-diffusion control, so expressivity is only shown at three hand-chosen points." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-elegans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

